    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d166">

                <pb facs="0297" n="189" sameAs="frus:frus1927v02/pg189"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00 Nanking/183</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Hankow</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lockhart</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Minister for Foreign Affairs of the Nationalist
                        Government</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Ch’en</hi>)<anchor n="56" xml:id="d166-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-04-11"><hi rendition="#italic">April 11,
                        1927</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Under instructions of the American
                    Government I am directed by the American Minister to present to you the
                    following terms (which are simultaneously being communicated to General Chiang
                    Kai-shek, Commander-in-Chief of the Nationalist Armies) for the prompt
                    settlement of the situation created by the outrages against American nationals
                    committed by Nationalist troops at Nanking on 24th of March last: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>Adequate punishment of Commanders of the troops responsible for the
                            murders, the personal injuries and indignities and the material damage
                            done as also of all persons found to be implicated.</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>Apology in writing by the Commander-in-Chief of the Nationalist Army
                            including an express written undertaking to refrain from all forms of
                            violence and agitation against foreign lives and property.</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>Complete reparation for the personal injuries and material damage
                            done.</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <pb facs="0298" n="190" xml:id="pg190"/>
                <p>Unless the Nationalist Authorities demonstrate to the satisfaction of the
                    interested Governments their intention to comply promptly with these terms the
                    said Governments will find themselves compelled to take such measures as they
                    consider appropriate.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">F. P. Lockhart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
